# ref-954cf87-collide-connected-false
# Upstream box3d issue #117: a joint created with collideConnected false must clear
# the contacts that already exist between the two bodies. Two dynamic unit boxes
# overlap at rest (gravity zero); one step forms a touching contact, then a revolute
# joint with collideConnected false is created before step 1. The contact count drops
# to 0 at step 1 and stays 0. Reference: vanilla float box3d at 954cf87; fixed:
# fixed3d on this branch (the port of step 3, src/joint.c).
# Observable: the per-step contact counter. It must be 1 at step 0 and 0 at steps 1+
#   in both engines; the two bodies' transform traces agree within tolerance for the
#   whole run (they are pushed apart by the first step, then held by the joint).
# Tolerance: twice the measured maximum divergence on this bench against float box3d
#   at 954cf87 (pos 2.98e-5, rot 7.04e-5, vel 7.12e-5, angvel 2.29e-4; contact count
#   exact). Values below 8*B3_FIXED_EPSILON are floored to it.
expect pos 0.0002 rot 0.0002 vel 0.0005 horizon 3 counts exact
world gravity 0 0 0 dt 1 60 substeps 4 steps 3
body dynamic position 0 0 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
body dynamic position 0.5 0 0 rotation 0 0 0 1 linvel 0 0 0 angvel 0 0 0
shape 0 box 0.5 0.5 0.5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
shape 1 box 0.5 0.5 0.5 density 1 friction 0.5 restitution 0
joint revolute 0 1 anchor 0 0 0 axis 0 0 1 collideConnected false at_step 1
